s handlers, and the default action that ends the process): handled true"] [69 1 "// and the call returns."] [72 1 "// signalTakenHook, when set, says a signal's handler is another module's (queue 220: faulthandler.register without"] [73 1 "// chain replaces the Python handler, as its sigaction does): the Python handler is not tripped."] [76 1 "// deliverSignal is the C handler: held when blocked, else tripped; the wakeup fd written."] [98 1 "// tripSignal marks n pending and wakes the main thread (trip_signal)."] [110 1 "// runPendingSignals is _PyErr_CheckSignalsTstate on the main thread: each tripped signal's Python handler"] [111 1 "// called with the signal and the running frame; an exception from one leaves the rest tripped for later."] [142 1 "// setOSHandler makes the process's action for n follow its Python handler and the mask: notified when a"] [143 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [167 3 "// SIG_DFL is the default action, also for a signal ignored at the start that Go's Reset leaves ignored"] [168 3 "// (py-mods-1122)"] [175 1 "// exitSigint is Modules/main.c's exit_sigint after an unhandled KeyboardInterrupt (queue 231): SIGINT's default action"] [176 1 "// restored and the signal sent to the process, so that its parent sees it killed by SIGINT; else exit status 130."] [182 38 "// delivered to this thread on the call's return; another one's at the latest here"] [187 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [188 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [189 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [204 3 "// blocked: pending when kill returns, as the kernel makes it (queue 231: sigpending right after saw nothing, the"] [205 3 "// signal still on its way through Go's handler thread)"] [215 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [229 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [248 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [249 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [270 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [271 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [316 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [322 4 "// a SIGHUP ignored at the process's start (nohup, a parent's SIG_IGN): SIG_IGN, as CPython's signal_get_set_handlers"] [323 4 "// reads it (py-mods-1122)"] [443 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [466 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [575 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [579 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [632 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [691 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd of another process times out here, harmlessly) handled"] [692 5 "// before the call returns, as the kernel delivers it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[51 82] [59 35] [93 26] [120 12] [120 22] [133 60] [163 22] [192 40] [209 50] [318 14] [318 24] [360 31] [375 14] [375 24] [377 39] [402 40] [424 26] [438 40] [449 63] [485 37] [502 32] [517 31] [559 37] [608 14] [608 24] [637 40] [679 35] [687 104] [694 16] [694 61]]} (go/file "builtins_signal.go" :imports [


